ca.pem - Aiven for MySQL CA certificate
=======================================

The MySQL connection to Aiven REQUIRES SSL. The application connects using a
CA certificate file named `ca.pem` in the project root.

How to get it:

1. Open your Aiven console: https://console.aiven.io
2. Select your MySQL service -> "Overview" page.
3. In the "Access" section find "CA Certificate".
4. Click to download the certificate file (it is a public certificate, safe
   to commit to the repository).
5. Save it in THIS project root with the exact name: ca.pem

Then set (Render dashboard / .env):

    MYSQL_SSL_CA=ca.pem

Notes:
- Do NOT invent or paste made-up certificate content - it must come from Aiven.
- ca.pem is NOT gitignored, so once downloaded it can be committed and Render
  will pick it up during the Docker build.
- Local XAMPP development does not need this file at all (SSL is skipped for
  localhost). If MYSQL_SSL_CA is unset and no ca.pem exists, the app runs
  without SSL exactly as before.
